+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report — num-bigint
+
+## 1. What Was Tested
+
+Property-based tests (hegel / `hegeltest` 0.28.2) were added for the core
+`BigInt`/`BigUint` arithmetic, conversion, and bit-manipulation APIs. Tests
+were appended to the existing integration test files rather than placed in a
+new file:
+
+- `tests/bigint.rs` — 15 properties: arithmetic/comparison differentials
+  against `i128`, string/byte/radix round-trips, division contracts, gcd/lcm,
+  pow, parse robustness and rejection.
+- `tests/bigint_bitwise.rs` — 5 properties: bitwise/shift/bit-query
+  differentials against `i128`, `set_bit`/`bit` consistency, `trailing_zeros`
+  contract.
+- `tests/modpow.rs` — 3 properties: `modpow` vs a naive oracle, the `modinv`
+  contract, and a pinned known-failure test for a real `modinv` bug (below).
+- `tests/roots.rs` — 2 properties: `nth_root`/`sqrt`/`cbrt` truncation
+  contracts for non-negative and negative inputs.
+- `tests/biguint.rs` — 1 property: `bits`/`count_ones`/`trailing_zeros` vs
+  `u128`.
+
+A shared `big_ints()` / `big_uints()` composite generator mixes full-range
+`i128`/`u128` draws (hitting `MIN`/`MAX`/`0` machine-word boundaries) with
+regex-generated decimal strings up to 81 digits (values far wider than any
+machine type, exercising multi-limb code paths).
+
+Setup note: `cargo add --dev hegeltest` required `--ignore-rust-version`
+(crate pins `rust-version = 1.60`; hegeltest's MSRV is 1.86). This is a
+dev-dependency-only MSRV concern.
+
+## 2. Properties and Oracles
+
+| Property | Oracle |
+|---|---|
+| `+ - * neg abs` on i64 operands | exact `i128` computation (widened, cannot overflow) |
+| `/ % div_mod_floor div_euclid rem_euclid` on full-range i128 | primitive `i128` checked ops and num-integer's independent primitive impl |
+| `Ord` | `i128::cmp` |
+| `to_str_radix`/`from_str_radix` round-trip, radix 2..=36 | identity, incl. negative/zero/81-digit values |
+| `Display`/`FromStr` round-trip | identity |
+| `Binary/Octal/LowerHex/UpperHex/Display` fmt impls | sibling API `to_str_radix(2/8/16/10)` |
+| signed-bytes and (sign, bytes) LE/BE round-trips | identity; LE == reversed BE |
+| `to_radix_le/be`/`from_radix_le/be` round-trip, radix 2..=256 | identity + all digits < radix |
+| `div_rem` (truncated) contract on wide values | `a == q*b + r`, `|r| < |b|`, `sign(r) == sign(a)` |
+| `div_mod_floor` contract on wide values | `a == q*b + r`, `|r| < |b|`, `sign(r) == sign(b)` |
+| `gcd`/`lcm` | gcd ≥ 0, divides both, `gcd(a,0) == |a|`, `gcd*lcm == |a*b|` |
+| `pow` | repeated multiplication (sign alternation, `0^0 == 1`) |
+| parse rejection | corrupting a valid radix string with `#` must yield `Err` |
+| parse robustness | arbitrary text never panics (`from_str_radix`, `parse_bytes`, `FromStr`) |
+| `& | ^ !`, `<< >>`, `bit()` | two's-complement `i128` computation (incl. sign-bit saturation past bit 127) |
+| `set_bit`/`bit` | read-back, other bits unchanged, arithmetic delta is exactly `±2^i` or `0` |
+| `trailing_zeros` | `None` iff zero; bits below clear, bit at index set, shifted-down value odd |
+| `bits`/`count_ones`/`trailing_zeros` (BigUint) | `u128` primitives |
+| `modpow` (small exponents, both modulus signs) | naive repeated multiply with `mod_floor` + documented result interval |
+| `modinv` | exists iff `gcd == 1`; `a*x ≡ 1 (mod m)`; documented `mod_floor` interval |
+| `nth_root`/`sqrt`/`cbrt` | truncation bracket `r^n <= x < (r+1)^n` (and mirrored for negative x, odd n) |
+
+## 3. Bug Found (real, pinned, not fixed)
+
+**`BigInt::modinv` violates its documented result interval when the modulus
+is `1` or `-1`.**
+
+- Docs (`src/bigint.rs`): "The solution will be in the interval
+  `[0, modulus)` for `modulus > 0`, or in the interval `(modulus, 0]` for
+  `modulus < 0`". For `m == 1` the only legal answer is `0`; likewise for
+  `m == -1`.
+- Actual: `BigInt::from(-1).modinv(&BigInt::from(1)) == Some(1)` and
+  `BigInt::from(1).modinv(&BigInt::from(-1)) == Some(-1)`.
+- Mechanism: the sign fixup in `BigInt::modinv` computes
+  `&modulus.data - result` when `self` and `modulus` have differing signs.
+  The unsigned inverse `result` is `0` exactly when `|m| == 1`, so the fixup
+  returns `|m|` (with sign) instead of the reduced value `0`. The affected
+  combinations are (negative self, `m == 1`) and (non-negative self,
+  `m == -1`); same-sign combinations are unaffected.
+- Discovered by `hegel_modinv_contract`, shrunk to `a = -1, m = 1`.
+- Pinned by `tests/modpow.rs::hegel_modinv_unit_modulus_interval`, whose
+  generator makes **every** drawn case hit the bug, so it fails
+  deterministically on each run (KNOWN FAILURE comment in the test). The
+  sibling `hegel_modinv_contract` excludes `|m| == 1` with a comment
+  referencing the pin, and stays green for everything else.
+
+## 4. Verification (Run and Reflect)
+
+- **Liveness:** four assertions were temporarily inverted — including ones
+  *inside guarded branches* (`checked_div` Some-branch of the i128
+  differential, the `Some(x)` branch of `modinv`, the `Some(tz)` branch of
+  `trailing_zeros`) — and all four failed with minimal shrunk counterexamples
+  (`0/1/2`-scale values), confirming both liveness and that the guarded
+  branches actually fire. The inversions were then reverted and the `.hegel/`
+  failure database removed.
+- **Exploratory 10x run:** all hegel tests were temporarily raised to
+  `test_cases = 1000` and re-run with an atomic case counter on a
+  representative test; the counter confirmed 1000+ executed cases. No new
+  failures appeared beyond the pinned `modinv` bug. Settings were reverted to
+  the default 100 cases for the committed tests.
+- **Final state:** `cargo test --tests --no-fail-fast` — 26 hegel tests, all
+  green except the single deterministic known-failure pin
+  (`hegel_modinv_unit_modulus_interval`). All 171 pre-existing tests still
+  pass.
+
+## 5. Gaps and Suggestions
+
+- The crate's existing randomized coverage is quickcheck/arbitrary *impls*
+  (feature-gated generators for downstream users) plus fixed fuzz regressions
+  in `tests/fuzzed.rs`; there were no in-repo property tests to port. The new
+  tests supplement, and do not replace, anything.
+- Not covered here: the feature-gated surfaces (`serde`, `rand_0_9/0_10`,
+  `quickcheck`, `arbitrary` impls) — serde round-trip and `RandBigInt` range
+  properties would be natural follow-ups; and `BigUint`-specific arithmetic
+  differentials (largely subsumed by the `BigInt` magnitude paths, but
+  `checked_sub`-style underflow behavior could be targeted).
+- The `modinv` unit-modulus bug is a one-line fix
+  (reduce `&modulus.data - result` when `result` is zero, or special-case
+  `|m| == 1`); it was deliberately left unfixed per the task instructions.
